
%% MGRAI
#grail-room
(room *)
(name *)	Grail Room
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You are standing in a small circular room with a pedestal. A set of
	stairs leads up, and passages leave to the east and west.
(from * go #west to #round-room)
(from * go #east to #narrow-crawlway)
(from * go #up to #temple)

%% TEMP1
#temple
(room *)
(name *)	Temple
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are in the west end of a large temple. On the south wall is an
	ancient inscription, probably a prayer in a long-forgotten language. The
	north wall is solid granite. The entrance at the west end of the room is
	through huge marble pillars.
(from * go #west to #grail-room)
(from * go #east to #altar)

%% TEMP2
#altar
(room *)
(name *)	Altar
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are in the east end of a large temple. In front of you is what
	appears to be an altar.
(from * go #west to #temple)

%% GRAIL
#grail
(* is #in #grail-room)
(name *)	grail
(item *)
(container *)
(openable *)
(dict *)	grail
(* size is 10)
(* capacity is 5)
(* awards 2 points on first take)
(* awards 5 points on return)
(appearance *)
	There is an extremely valuable \(perhaps original\) grail here.

%% PRAYE
#prayer
(* is #in #temple)
(name *)	prayer
(readable *)
(* is sacred)
(dict *)	inscr ancie old praye prayer
(descr *)
	The prayer is inscribed in an ancient script which is hardly remembered
	these days, much less understood. What little of it can be made out
	seems to be a phillipic against small insects, absent-mindedness, and
	the picking up and dropping of small objects. The final verse seems to
	consign trespassers to the land of the dead. All evidence indicates that
	the beliefs of the ancient Zorkers were obscure.

%% BELL
#bell
(* is #in #temple)
(name *)	brass bell
(item *)
(ringable *)
(appearance *)
	There is a small brass bell here.
(initial appearance *)
	Lying in a corner of the room is a small brass bell.

%% BOOK
#book
(* is #in #altar)
(name *)	black book
(item *)
(readable *)
(flammable *)
(dict *)	large prayer bible
(* size is 10)
(appearance *)
	There is a large black book here.
(initial appearance *)
	On the altar is a large black book, open to page 569.
(descr *)
	(div @headline) { COMMANDMENT \#12592 }
	Oh ye who go about saying unto each: "Hello sailor":(line)
	dost thou know the magnitude of thy sin before the gods? Yea, verily,
	thou shalt be ground between two stones. Shall the angry gods cast thy
	body into the whirlpool? Surely, thy eye shall be put out with a sharp
	stick! Even unto the ends of the earth shalt thou wander and unto the
	land of the dead shalt thou be sent at last. Surely thou shalt repent of
	thy cunning.
